    "abstract": "The paper gradually modernises a standard ResNet toward the design of a vision Transformer and discovers key components contributing to the performance gap. The resulting pure-ConvNet family, ConvNeXt, competes favourably with Transformers in accuracy and scalability, achieving 87.8% ImageNet top-1 and outperforming Swin Transformers on COCO detection and ADE20K segmentation while keeping ConvNet simplicity.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Modernising ResNet step by step (training recipe, macro design, ResNeXt-ify, inverted bottleneck, large kernels, micro design) closes the gap with Swin Transformers.",
      "ConvNeXt-T reaches 82.1% ImageNet-1K top-1 with 28.6M parameters and 4.5 GFLOPs.",
      "ConvNeXt-XL pretrained on ImageNet-22K reaches 87.8% top-1 at 384 px.",
      "ConvNeXt matches or outperforms Swin on COCO detection and ADE20K segmentation."
